  "description": "Program director: J. VanHorn The MS in Geographic Information Science program is suited for students who wish to gain expertise in geographic information systems and science (GIS/GISc) for a wide range of professional applications. The program is a good fit for those who want to begin or advance their career in GIS in the public or private sector. Applicants for the MS in Geographic Information Science who have successfully completed the equivalent courses for the GIS certificate (GEO 560, GEO 561, GEO 562) at another accredited academic institution may be eligible for advanced standing. These courses will be credited toward the MS in Geographic Information Science program, allowing students to accelerate their time to completion. If the amount of credit transferred is less than 12 credit hours, students may be required to take GEO 570 - Special Topics in GIS in order to reach the required 30 credit hours for the program.",
